   "title": "NH State Parks - Recreational Rail Trails",
   "text": "Employment\nGroup Use & Events\nTrails Bureau\nPay a Ticket\nMake a Donation\nStore\nSearch\nPARKS & TRAILS\nCAMPING & LODGING\nTHINGS TO DO\nFEES & RESERVATIONS\nABOUT US\nSkip to main content\nSUGAR RIVER RECREATIONAL RAIL TRAIL\nActivities and Amenities\nThis 9 mile trail begins at the Newport Recreation Department on Belknap Ave in Newport and ends at Washington Street in Claremont. The trail boasts two historic covered bridges and meanders along the Sugar River.\nSugar River Recreational Rail Trail Map\nParking Areas\nClaremont: OHRV trailhead on south side of Rt 103. 398-394 Washington St, Claremont (43.365535, -72.302509). Google maps has “Sugar River Trail, ORV Trailhead” on the map for this parking lot.\nNewport: Green Crow parking at 601-613 John Stark highway off Rt. 11/103. Sign with the “green crow” marks where to turn. Park alongside of highway as you go down under the bridge. Not much parking here, could not have a trailer to load/unload. (43.363045, -72.225993)\nNewport: Limited parking on side of road on Oak St, Newport. (43.386010, -72.208441). Not enough room for trailers.\nNewport: Newport Trail head is next to Newport Recreation Department at 65 Belknap Ave, Newport. Limited parking on side of building. Go behind building to access dirt lot near gate (43.367012, -72.179297). There is a propane truck fill up station next to lot that has to be shared.\nOrganizations that work in with the Bureau of Trails to help maintain this trail are:\nCrescent Lake Regional Sno-Riders Shugah Valley Snow Riders, Inc.\nNH State Parks\nExplore our 94 properties: parks, campgrounds, beaches, natural areas, waysides, historic sites and recreational trails.\nNH State Parks License Plate\nCommissions and Committees\nPark Proposals & RFPs\nBlog\nContact Us\nRight-to-Know (RSA 91-A) Requests\n© 2026 NH Department of Natural and Cultural Resources 172 Pembroke Road Concord, NH 03301\nEN",
